# Standalone ESM scripts must keep LF in the working tree.
#
# Two things break otherwise. Vitest fails to transform a CRLF .mjs with
# "Invalid or unexpected token" — Node imports the same file happily, so the
# failure only shows up in the test run. And a shebang whose line ends in CRLF
# makes the script unrunnable on Linux, because the kernel looks for
# "/usr/bin/env node\r".
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.d.mts text eol=lf
